    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured MA worked solutions. No earlier submissions or grades were supplied; evidence is from worked solutions only. q-143789: E[X^3]=0+2/9+8/2=38/9. q-143827: E[X^4]=0.25+16(0.6)+81(0.1)+256(0.05)=30.75; the source's phrase 'each squared value' is an authored prose error—the calculation correctly uses fourth powers. q-109312: linearity gives 3(27)-2(5)+4=75. q-110011: expanding the square gives 4(4)-32(1)+64=48. q-85596: y'=4√x, so the length is [(1+16x)^(3/2)/24] from 0 to 3, namely (343-1)/24=57/4; the source incorrectly writes dx in one integral after substituting u, but its evaluation and final answer are correct. q-122394: the chosen curve has derivative 1/(1+x^2), whose square gives the stated arc-length integrand. q-36055: the first-row minors are -30 and 69, giving (-3)(-30)-5(69)=-255. q-130822: deleting row 2 and column 2 gives the selected determinant; its evaluated value is -16-56√3, equivalent to the selected expression. q-42106: third-row expansion gives -2 times a minor of 6, hence -12. q-130035: third-row expansion gives -2 times a minor of 16, hence -32. For each variance, use E[X^2]-E[X]^2: q-129108 gives 32-3^2=23; q-84023 gives 41/6-(7/3)^2=25/18; q-129040 gives 58-7^2=9; q-129043 gives 105.5-10^2=5.5; q-84200 gives 87/8-3^2=15/8; q-84208 gives 55/9-(19/9)^2=134/81. The two incidental source errors do not change the confirmed final answers.",
